- op: discuss  # 5ae9
  at: '2026-04-18T01:39:21Z'  # 5ae9
  by: agent  # 5ae9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5ae9
  clock: 4  # 5ae9
  nonce: 5ae9  # 5ae9
  message: "Incorporating WI-zakub lessons into this item's scope:\n\n1. Both open questions in the original description are now answered — no pre-coding investigation needed:\n   - \"How is trait-dispatch represented in SCIP relationships?\" — It is NOT. rust-analyzer leaves the SCIP Relationship field empty (WI-zakub §1). Trait-resolved method references are encoded inside the symbol descriptor string itself (e.g., \"rust-analyzer cargo crate version impl#[T][Trait]method()\"). The shim must parse the descriptor syntax to recover implementation_of / defined_by relationships; a Rust-specific post-processing step IS required at the shim's output layer, even though the shim body stays language-agnostic. Proposed split: shim emits Symbol/Edge objects with the raw SCIP symbol string in a provenance field; an optional \"descriptor decoder\" (rust_analyzer-package-local) walks the provenance and adds `implements` / `defined_in` Edges for trait method dispatches.\n   - \"Are macro-expanded items in SCIP tagged with original or synthetic spans?\" — Expansion-generated items are ABSENT from the SCIP index entirely (WI-zakub §2); only the macro-invocation site appears, with original-source spans. The shim therefore emits no synthetic symbols for #[tokio::main], #[wasm_bindgen], #[napi], #[pyo3] expansions. Existing proc-macro FFI linkers (wasm_bindgen.py, napi.py, pyo3) retain sole authority over those constructs; document this carve-out in the shim's module docstring so the downstream question \"why doesn't SCIP see my #[napi] function?\" has an in-tree answer.\n\n2. Span semantics — SCIP Occurrence.range is line/col in UTF-8 column units (WI-zakub §3). Map directly to hypergumbo's Span dataclass (also line/col); no byte-offset conversion needed. Add a validation test that a SCIP-originated Symbol's span round-trips through hypergumbo's Span.from_dict / to_dict unchanged.\n\n3. Test fixture scale — WI-zakub's ripgrep trial produced a 7.3MB SCIP file from a 4.3MB crate. That's usable as an end-to-end integration test target but too large for routine unit tests. Recorded fixtures should be small single-file crates (~10KB SCIP) for the shim's unit tests; ripgrep-scale belongs in a marker-gated integration test run less frequently.\n\n4. Opt-in gating — the shim itself has no runtime cost when unused, but the package must not import rust-analyzer at module-load time. Any invocation of the rust-analyzer binary stays behind WI-nohah's optional-dep pattern: graceful degrade, explicit --enable-rust-analyzer flag, clear warning on invocation about the 10x+ wall-time cost relative to rust.py.\n\n5. Warning on empty Relationship field — the shim should log a one-time info message when a SCIP index has zero non-empty Relationship entries (currently true for all rust-analyzer output). Otherwise a user debugging \"why are no `implements` edges appearing from SCIP?\" will have no hint that rust-analyzer populates the info elsewhere. The message should point to the Rust-specific descriptor-decoder post-processor.\n\nNo change to the item's status — these are scope clarifications that unblock implementation, not scope additions. Ready to move from todo_soft to active work whenever the upstream package scaffold (WI-duzul) lands."  # 5ae9
- op: discuss  # 2212
  at: '2026-04-19T15:42:41Z'  # 2212
  by: agent  # 2212
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2212
  clock: 5  # 2212
  nonce: '2212'  # 2212
  message: "Phase 1 shipped: SCIP symbol-string descriptor parser merged in commit 12846b608 on dev (PR auto-merged). New module hypergumbo_core.scip.descriptor exposes parse_scip_symbol → frozen ScipSymbol dataclass with 8-kind DescriptorKind enum (NAMESPACE/TYPE/TERM/META/METHOD/MACRO/TYPE_PARAMETER/PARAMETER). Covers the WI-zakub trait-dispatch descriptor shape (impl#[T][Trait]method().) which is where rust-analyzer encodes trait resolution instead of SCIP Relationship. No protobuf dependency introduced — parser operates on wire strings directly. 30 tests, 100% coverage, per-package isolation PASSED.\n\nRemaining WI-mafut scope (deferred to Phase 2+, all still in this item):\n- Walk scip.proto Index.documents and emit hypergumbo Symbol objects (Document.language → Symbol.language; Document.relative_path → Symbol.path; Occurrence range → Symbol.span; SymbolInformation.symbol via parse_scip_symbol for name/kind)\n- Emit Edge objects from Occurrences (def/ref roles → call-graph edges)\n- Emit Edge objects from SymbolInformation.relationships (implements / has_type) and log one-time info warning when Relationships set is empty index-wide (rust-analyzer always empty per WI-zakub §1)\n- Add the scip-proto optional dependency gate (pyproject.toml extras_require) — coordinate with WI-duzul which will be the first caller\n\nLeaving status todo_soft; Phase 2 picks up from here."  # 2212
- op: discuss  # 47ff
  at: '2026-04-19T15:54:45Z'  # 47ff
  by: agent  # 47ff
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 47ff
  clock: 6  # 47ff
  nonce: 47ff  # 47ff
  message: "Phase 2 dependency research (blocker-de-risking for next session):\n\nProbed PyPI for a ready-made SCIP protobuf Python binding — none exists. Checked scip (occupied by an unrelated Scalable Cytometry Image Processing project), scip-python, sourcegraph-scip, scip-pb, scip-protobuf, scip-index, scip-pb2 — all 404 except the cytometry squatter. So Phase 2 cannot just 'add scip-proto to optional-deps' — there is no such package.\n\nThree viable paths for Phase 2:\n  A) Vendor Sourcegraph's scip.proto file and run 'protoc --python_out' at install time. Adds protobuf-compiler build-time dep. Rejected-ish: fragile install story.\n  B) Vendor pre-generated scip_pb2.py (one file, ~30KB) into packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/scip/_generated/. Keep it checked in; regenerate via a scripts/build-scip-proto when scip.proto version bumps. Simple and self-contained. Preferred.\n  C) Hand-roll minimal protobuf parsing for just the Document/SymbolInformation/Occurrence/Relationship messages we consume. Skinny (SCIP schema is small) but duplicates work that protoc already does correctly. Use only if (B) proves unworkable.\n\nRecommendation for Phase 2: option B. scip.proto lives at github.com/sourcegraph/scip/blob/main/scip.proto (pinned to a specific commit in the vendoring script). The 'protobuf' runtime is already an indirect dep of several things hypergumbo-core already ships (google.protobuf importable today per this session's python -c check). No new install-time toolchain needed.\n\nRecording this now so the next session doesn't re-do the PyPI probe."  # 47ff
