- op: discuss  # b4dc
  at: '2026-04-20T01:14:49Z'  # b4dc
  by: agent  # b4dc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b4dc
  clock: 8  # b4dc
  nonce: b4dc  # b4dc
  message: "Acknowledged path B — vendoring a pinned scip.proto + pre-generated scip_pb2.py under packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/scip/_generated/.\n\nPhase 2 plan now concrete:\n\n1. Add scripts/build-scip-proto: curls scip.proto from github.com/sourcegraph/scip at a pinned commit SHA (record SHA in a constant at the top of the script + in _generated/SOURCE_COMMIT.txt), runs protoc --python_out against the downloaded file, emits _generated/scip_pb2.py. Script is developer-run (not CI-run); the generated file is checked in. Allowlist check: github.com / raw.githubusercontent.com for the curl.\n\n2. _generated/ layout: __init__.py (empty), scip_pb2.py (generated), SOURCE_COMMIT.txt (pinned SHA for reproducibility). No hand edits to scip_pb2.py; regenerate via the build script when the SHA bumps.\n\n3. hypergumbo_core.scip.index (new module): walks scip_pb2.Index.documents, emits hypergumbo Symbol objects. Uses Phase 1 parse_scip_symbol for the descriptor field. Maps Document.language → Symbol.language, Document.relative_path → Symbol.path, Occurrence.range → Span(line, col) (UTF-8 col units per WI-zakub §3 — direct assignment, no conversion).\n\n4. hypergumbo_core.scip.edges (new module): emits Edge objects. Two sources: Occurrence def/ref roles → call-graph edges; SymbolInformation.relationships → implements / has_type / defined_in edges. One-time INFO log when every SymbolInformation.relationships is empty (rust-analyzer case per WI-zakub §1) pointing to the descriptor decoder.\n\n5. Runtime protobuf dep: 'protobuf' is already importable in the hypergumbo-core env (verified Phase 2 research turn). No new install-time toolchain. If a fresh install surfaces a missing protobuf, add it to pyproject.toml extras_require under a 'scip' extra; keep _generated/scip_pb2.py's import at module level so the error surfaces at import, not runtime.\n\n6. Tests: unit tests use recorded SCIP fixtures (~10KB single-file crates, checked in). Integration test gated by a marker for ripgrep-scale fixtures. 100% coverage on the shim; # pragma: no cover on defensive branches per AGENTS.md.\n\nStatus stays todo_soft; will start Phase 2 once the current reply-first cycle clears. No scope change."  # b4dc
